<title>ZAMBIA: PRESS DIGEST - Zambia - Oct 17.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Zambia - Oct 17.</headline>
<dateline>LUSAKA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the leading stories in the Zambian press on Thursday.</p>
<p>Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>TIMES OF ZAMBIA</p>
<p>- Striking teachers in Lusaka and the Copperbelt called off a six-week strike over pay grievances.</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>THE POST</p>
<p>- The opposition Liberal Progressive Front said President Frederick Chiluba was likely to declare a state of emergency to allow him to remain in office after October 31, when parliament's five-year term ends.</p>
<p>- Lusaka newsroom +2601 222689</p>
